 "note": "Quick, Draw! diving board 6443723384684544: a long plank with a rounded pedestal under its left end (stroke 0, one loop), and a small stick person standing at the plank's right tip: head loop (stroke 1), neck-to-hip line ending in the left leg (stroke 2), a separate right leg (stroke 3), and one straight arm line across the shoulders (stroke 4; a vertex was added at the shoulder, on the line, so each arm can turn). The person is the swimmer in the film: the root places the person by the top of the head and the feet, at one size for the whole shot, and shortens the drawing a little along that line when he crouches. Each arm turns at the shoulder to follow his arms (down at his sides, out level, up in a V); each leg turns at the hip. The board (stroke 0) is drawn at about a third of the person's scale and turns about his feet so that its far end stays on the pose's 'back' point: when his feet press the tip down, the plank tilts, as the real board flexes.",
